$ fosscut capabilities
API 0.1.0  project format 0.14.0
commands:
  adjustment.add Add an adjustment layer: a clip on a video track whose effects (and opacity) apply to every picture below it for its time range, such as one grade over a whole sequence. Add effects with effects here or effect.add later.
  animation.set  Animate a clip in (fade, slide_left/right/up/down, zoom_in, zoom_out, spin, pop, drop), out (the same, reversed), or with a repeating combo (pulse, swing, float, shake); clear removes them. Animations move placement and opacity on top of keyframes.
  captions.add   Caption timed words: page them into caption clips (a few words per page, split at sentence ends and pauses) on a caption track, optionally styled with a preset. Never overwrites unless replace is set.
  captions.edit  Change one caption page: new timed words, new wording that keeps the page's timing, which words are emphasised, or its translation line (bilingual captions).
  captions.style Set how a caption track's captions look and move: a built-in preset, a style patch, or both.
  clip.add       Place a media asset (or, with compound, a compound timeline) on a track. Never overwrites: fails with fosscut.clip.overlap if the range is taken.
  clip.align     Align a clip on the canvas: put the visible part of its picture against the left, right, top or bottom edge, or centre it, taking its scale, crop, flips and rotation into account. Text and captions can only be centred.
  clip.canvas    Fill the canvas around video or image clips whose picture does not cover it (a 16:9 shot in a vertical video): with their own picture blurred to cover, or a colour; no fill removes it. Several clips at once.
  clip.compound  Make a compound clip: move chosen clips into a new compound timeline (keeping their tracks and timing) and put one clip showing it in their place, on the lowest of their video tracks. Trim, speed, effects and transitions then apply to it as a whole.
  clip.copy_attributes Paste attributes: copy one clip's placement, crop, opacity, blend mode, volume and sound settings, effects, masks or animations (with their keyframes) to other clips, keeping their media. Effects and masks skip audio clips.
  clip.decompose Break a compound clip apart: put the part of its timeline it shows back in its place, clip by clip, on tracks of the same kinds. The compound timeline goes when nothing else shows it. The compound clip must have no speed, effects, masks, keyframes or placement of its own.
  clip.extract_audio Extract a video clip's sound into an audio clip of its own, on the first audio track free over its span (or a new one), grouped with the video so they stay in sync. The video clip is no longer heard; clip.restore_audio undoes it.
  clip.freeze    Insert a freeze frame: hold the frame of a video clip at a time for a duration (two seconds by default), splitting the clip there and moving what follows on its track later. The held frame is silent.
  clip.group     Group two or more clips of a timeline so clip.move, clip.split, clip.trim and clip.remove edit them together (pass linked: false to edit one). They leave any group they were in.
  clip.move      Move a clip to a new position and/or a compatible track; its group moves by the same time unless linked: false. Never overwrites: fails with fosscut.clip.overlap.
  clip.remove    Remove a clip, and its group unless linked: false. Clips on the primary (lowest) video track need allow_destructive; ripple closes the gap.
  clip.replace   Replace a clip's media with another asset, keeping its place, length, speed, effects, masks, keyframes and animations. The new media must be long enough (fosscut.clip.source_range).
  clip.restore_audio Put a video clip's extracted sound back: remove the audio clips of its group that play the same media, and hear the video clip again.
  clip.set       Set a clip's properties by path: transform.position, transform.scale, transform.stretch (non-uniform), transform.rotation, transform.flip_horizontal and flip_vertical (mirror), crop.left/right/top/bottom, opacity, blend (multiply, screen, overlay and others), enabled (false deactivates), volume, audio.pan, audio.fade_in, audio.fade_out, audio.channels (fill channel). Position and scale are relative to the canvas and the fitted size. Properties with keyframes are set with keyframe.set instead.
  clip.speed     Change a video, audio or compound clip's speed: a constant rate (0.05 to 100), a speed curve or preset (montage, hero, bullet, jump_cut, flash_in, flash_out), reverse, pitch (preserve or shift) and smooth slow motion (interpolate blend). The clip keeps the media it plays, so faster clips get shorter; ripple moves the clips after it.
  clip.split     Split a clip at a timeline position. The left part keeps the id; the right part gets a new id and continues the source. Clips of its group spanning the time split too unless linked: false.
  clip.trim      Move a clip's start or end edge: trim it shorter, or extend it into more of its media. The picture under the rest of the clip stays put. Never overwrites: fails with fosscut.clip.overlap, or fosscut.clip.source_range past the media. With ripple the clip keeps its start and later clips move by the change in length (delete left or right). Group members sharing the edge trim too unless linked: false.
  clip.ungroup   Take clips out of their groups, so each edits on its own again.
  clips.paste    Paste clips copied with the clips.copy query at a time, keeping their arrangement: new ids, the same media, effects, masks and keyframes, and groups among them kept. Never overwrites: fails with fosscut.clip.overlap.
  effect.add     Add an effect to a clip: to its picture (color.adjust for exposure, white balance, contrast, tone and saturation, color.curves, color.hsl, color.wheels, color.lut, color.vignette, blur.gaussian, detail.sharpen, stylize.grain and others) or to its sound (audio.denoise, audio.enhance_voice, audio.vocals to isolate or remove a centred voice). Effects apply in order; on an adjustment clip picture effects apply to everything below it. capabilities lists every type with its parameters.
  effect.copy    Apply one clip's effects (with their keyframes) to other clips, replacing theirs or, with append, after them: the way to grade every clip alike.
  effect.move    Move an effect to another position in its clip's order; effects apply first to last.
  effect.remove  Remove an effect and its keyframes from a clip.
  effect.set     Change an effect's parameters, reset some to their defaults, or bypass it (enabled: false). Parameters with keyframes are set with keyframe.set as effects.<id>.<param>.
  history.redo   Redo the most recently undone transaction. Must be the only command in its request.
  history.undo   Undo the most recent committed transaction. Must be the only command in its request.
  keyframe.remove Remove a keyframe of a clip property at a time, or all of its keyframes (all: true), which stops the animation; with all and a time, the property keeps the value it had then.
  keyframe.set   Animate a clip property: add a keyframe at a time (or replace the one there) with a value and an easing (linear, hold, ease_in, ease_out, ease_in_out or a Bezier). Between keyframes the value moves along the easing; before the first and after the last it holds. Animatable: transform.position, transform.scale, transform.stretch, transform.rotation, crop edges, opacity, volume, audio.pan, numeric effect parameters as effects.<id>.<param>, and mask placement as masks.<id>.<property>.
  keyframe.set_all Replace every keyframe of a clip property with a list of offsets from the clip's start and values, in one step: for motion measured by stabilization or tracking, or any animation planned whole.
  look.apply     Apply a built-in look (a filter such as warm, cool, teal_orange, vintage, noir, faded, vivid) as ordinary effects the clip owns, so it can be adjusted afterwards.
  marker.add     Add a marker to a timeline at a time, with an optional name and color: a beat, a cue, a note to come back to.
  marker.remove  Remove a marker.
  marker.set     Move a marker, or change its name or color.
  mask.add       Add a mask to a clip's picture: rectangle (round corners), ellipse, linear, mirror (a band), star, heart, path (pen, with Bezier handles), text or brush (painted strokes), placed by center and size as fractions of the picture, with rotation, feather, expansion and invert. Several masks combine in order (add, subtract, intersect); on an adjustment clip they limit where its effects apply.
  mask.remove    Remove a mask and its keyframes from a clip.
  mask.set       Change a mask: shape, placement (center, size, rotation), feather, expansion, roundness, invert, mode, path points, text or brush strokes, or turn it off (enabled: false). Animated values are set with keyframe.set as masks.<id>.<property>.
  media.add      Add a probed media file to the media table (front ends call this after probing; the CLI's `media import` does both).
  media.folder   Add, rename (or move) or remove a media bin folder. Removing one moves its assets and subfolders up to its parent; assets are never removed.
  media.move     Put assets in a media bin folder such as B-roll/Day 1 (created when missing), or back at the top level.
  media.relink   Point an asset at its file's new location (front ends measure the file; the CLI's media relink and the MCP media_import with relink do both). The content must be the same file (fosscut.asset.identity_mismatch); for other media use media.replace.
  media.remove   Remove an asset from the media bin (never the file). An asset that clips show fails with fosscut.asset.in_use, unless remove_clips (with allow_destructive) removes them too.
  media.rename   Rename an asset in the media bin. Only the display name changes, not the file.
  media.replace  Replace an asset with another in every clip that shows it, keeping each clip's place, length and source position. The new media must be long enough (fosscut.clip.source_range). The old asset stays in the bin.
  multicam.create Make a multicam clip from angles recorded at the same time: a compound clip whose timeline holds each angle on its own track, lined up by their offsets, with one angle's sound. Cut between angles with multicam.switch.
  multicam.switch Cut a multicam clip to another angle from a time on: it splits there and the part after shows the angle (by number or track id).
  shape.add      Draw a shape (rectangle, ellipse, star, heart, a pen path), a sticker (badges, buttons, arrows, speech bubbles, check marks) or a background (solid or gradient) from the built-in library, with its fill, gradient, outline and label. Backgrounds go below the footage, other shapes above it.
  shape.set      Change a shape clip's outline, size, roundness, fill, gradient, outline or label by a merge patch.
  template.apply Build a new timeline from a project template (vertical-promo, quote-card, photo-montage, product-reveal, talking-head-intro) with your media in its slots and your lines in its titles; everything it adds stays editable.
  text.add       Add a text clip: a style or preset (outline, shadow, boxes, glow, spacing, case, underline, project fonts), spans that restyle parts, and a reveal (typewriter, word by word, line by line). Never overwrites: fails with fosscut.clip.overlap if the range is taken.
  text.preset_remove Remove a text preset saved in the project; clips styled with it keep their style.
  text.preset_save Save a text clip's style (or a given style) as a named preset of the project, to reuse with preset in text.add and text.set.
  text.set       Change a text clip: its text, a preset, a style patch (font, size, colour, bold, italic, underline, case, alignment, letter and line spacing, outline, box, shadow, glow), its spans or its reveal.
  text.template  Add a title template (lower-third, headline, chapter, quote, callout, end-card) as a styled, animated text clip with your lines.
  timeline.add   Add a timeline to the project: empty, or a new timeline from chosen media placed one after another, with the canvas and rate of the first video unless given. primary makes it the one commands and exports use by default.
  timeline.duplicate Copy a timeline, for example onto a 1080x1920 canvas for a vertical version; fit fill scales the pictures to cover the new canvas. The original stays as it is.
  timeline.remove Remove a timeline (allow_destructive when it has clips). A project keeps at least one timeline; removing the primary one makes the next primary.
  timeline.remove_ranges Cut time ranges (pauses, fillers, retakes) out of every track at once and close the gaps, keeping picture, sound and captions in sync. Cutting the primary video track needs allow_destructive.
  timeline.rename Rename a timeline.
  timeline.set_primary Make a timeline the primary one: the timeline the app shows and commands, frames and exports use when given no timeline.
  timeline.split Split all: cut every clip under a time on every unlocked track (or the tracks named) in one step. Grouped clips' right parts form new groups.
  track.add      Add an empty video, audio or text track; later tracks draw on top of earlier ones.
  transition.remove Remove the transition from a clip into the next one: a plain cut again.
  transition.set Add or replace the transition from a clip into the next clip on its track (they must touch): dissolve, dip (to a color), wipe, slide, push (with a direction), zoom, blur, iris, clock or spin, centred on the cut. The sound crossfades with it.
queries:
  capabilities   Commands, queries, their JSON Schemas, the request envelope, time formats and error codes.
  clips.copy     Copy clips as documents (media, effects, masks, keyframes, groups) to pass to clips.paste, in this project or another with the same media.
  history.list   Most recent operation log entries, newest first.
  media.list     Assets in the media table with durations and stream details.
  project.info   Project name, revision, timelines and undo state.
  timeline.read  Agent-oriented view of a timeline: tracks and clips with frames, timecode and seconds.
operations:
  export.start         Render a timeline to a video or audio file with a preset, then verify the file by probing it.
  media.analyze        Measure an asset's loudness, silences and shot cuts, or transcribe its speech with word timings, on this machine; results are cached by content.
  captions.generate    Caption the clips of a track word by word from their cached transcripts, as pages on a caption track with a preset look; one undoable step.
  captions.import      Add caption pages from an SRT subtitle file, one page per cue with its lines kept.
  captions.export      Write a caption track to an SRT subtitle file, one cue per page.
  color.auto           Measure a video or image clip's picture and add a color.adjust effect that corrects its white balance, brightness and levels; one undoable step.
  color.match          Measure two clips and add a color.adjust effect to the first that brings its balance, brightness, contrast and saturation close to the second; one undoable step.
  audio.normalize      Measure clips' loudness as they play (ITU-R BS.1770) and set their volumes to reach a target with peaks under a ceiling, adding an audio.limiter where needed; one undoable step.
  library.add          Add an item of FossCut's own library: a sound or music loop (written into the bundle and imported), a shape, sticker, background, title or project template, a text or caption style, or a look; one undoable step.
  clip.split_scenes    Measure the shot cuts in a video clip's media (cached by content) and split the clip at them, so each shot is a clip of its own; one undoable step.
  clip.stabilize       Measure how the camera moved in a video clip and key its position, rotation and scale to cancel the shake, with one zoom up to 1.5 that hides the moving edges; one undoable step.
  clip.track           Follow a region of a video clip's picture from a time on and key one of its masks, or another clip such as a title or sticker, to move with it; one undoable step.
  multicam.sync        Measure how far apart angles recorded at the same time started, from their sound, as the offsets of multicam.create (which multicam create measures itself unless given offsets).
  record.start         Record a voiceover (48 kHz WAV), a camera or the screen into the bundle's recordings folder through the same encoders and checks as exports, then import it; stops after a duration or when asked, keeping what was recorded.
  preferences.edit     Read or change the user's preferences: editing and timeline defaults the CLI and the app fill requests with, performance and cache settings (ADR-0031); agents read them with the query preferences.read.
  media.proxy          Make a smaller ProRes Proxy copy of a video asset in FossCut's cache for the desktop preview; exports, frame grabs and contact sheets always read the original.
  media.remux          Copy a video asset in a hard-to-seek container (MPEG-TS, MPEG-PS, AVI, FLV) into QuickTime in FossCut's cache, without re-encoding, for the desktop preview.
  cache.clear          Report the size of FossCut's caches (analysis, proxies, remuxed copies, rendered frames), empty them, or clean them by the cache preferences; everything in them is made again when needed.
  update.check         Ask GitHub once for the latest FossCut release and say whether it is newer; nothing about the user is sent and nothing is installed.
  models.install       Download a model an analyzer needs (speech for transcript) after the user agrees to its size and license; it is verified by SHA-256.
  frame.grab           Render one frame of a timeline as a PNG image, exactly as an export shows it.
  frame.contact_sheet  Render frames spread evenly over a timeline into one PNG grid, to check an edit at a glance.
analyzers:
  loudness       Integrated loudness in LUFS (ITU-R BS.1770-4) and sample peak in dBFS.
  silences       Ranges whose level stays below a threshold for at least a minimum duration: pauses to cut or keep.
  scenes         Hard shot cuts with their frame, time and confidence.
  transcript     Speech as words with timings, filler candidates and pauses, recognised locally by whisper.cpp; needs an installed speech model and must be named.
models (fosscut models install <name>):
  whisper-large-v3-turbo  1624.6 MB  multilingual not installed
  whisper-small            487.6 MB  multilingual not installed
  whisper-base.en          148.0 MB  en           not installed
  whisper-tiny.en           77.7 MB  en           not installed
export presets:
  mp4-h264       H.264 and AAC in MP4: plays everywhere (hardware encoder)
  mp4-hevc       HEVC and AAC in MP4: smaller files (hardware encoder)
  mp4-av1        AV1 and AAC in MP4: small files, modern players
  mov-prores     ProRes 422 and AAC in QuickTime: for other editors
  mov-prores-proxy ProRes 422 Proxy and 24-bit PCM in QuickTime: light files for offline editing
  mov-prores-lt  ProRes 422 LT and 24-bit PCM in QuickTime: a lighter intermediate
  mov-prores-hq  ProRes 422 HQ and 24-bit PCM in QuickTime: for masters
  mov-prores-4444 ProRes 4444 with alpha and 24-bit PCM in QuickTime: for graphics and compositing
  webm-vp9       VP9 and Opus in WebM: for the web
  gif            Animated GIF, looping, no sound: pick a small size and frame rate
  m4a-aac        AAC audio only
  mp3            MP3 audio only: plays everywhere (LAME encoder)
  wav            16-bit PCM audio only in WAV: uncompressed
  wav-24         24-bit PCM audio only in WAV: uncompressed, for mastering
  flac           FLAC audio only: lossless 16-bit, about half the size of WAV
